Serve a plugin-resolved file from disk when no load hook claims it.

Rollup's contract is that resolveId returning a path means that file is the
module, and a load hook returning nothing means read it from disk. oj_server
implemented only the second half, so a plugin that maps bare specifiers to
paths without also serving their contents got a 404 for every module it
resolved correctly.

That is how a node_modules tree outside the app root is reached at all: the
on-disk resolver walks up from the importer, and a build system that keeps
node_modules out of the source tree has nothing there for it to find.

Upstreamable as-is; carried here so the dev server works today.

--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
     body::Body,
     extract::{ws::Message, Query, State, WebSocketUpgrade},
     http::{header, HeaderMap, Method, StatusCode, Uri},
-    response::{IntoResponse, Response},
+    response::{IntoResponse, Redirect, Response},
     routing::{get, post},
     Router,
 };
@@ -3120,6 +3120,30 @@
     let source = match host.load(&id).await {
         Ok(Some(src)) => src,
         Ok(None) => {
+            // Rollup's contract, which the plugin host is otherwise faithful to:
+            // `resolveId` returning a path means "that file is the module", and a
+            // `load` that returns nothing means "read it from disk". Only the
+            // second half was implemented here, so a plugin that maps specifiers
+            // to paths without also serving their contents -- which is what a
+            // resolver plugin is -- got a 404 for every module it resolved
+            // correctly.
+            //
+            // This is how a package tree outside the app root is reached at all:
+            // the on-disk resolver walks up from the importer, and a build system
+            // that keeps node_modules out of the source tree has nothing there
+            // for it to find. Serving the resolved file through the normal URL
+            // keeps every downstream behaviour (fs.allow, partial bundling, the
+            // specifier rewriting inside it) the same as for any other dep.
+            let resolved = Path::new(&id);
+            if resolved.is_absolute() && resolved.is_file() {
+                state
+                    .fs_allow
+                    .lock()
+                    .unwrap()
+                    .insert(package_root(resolved));
+                let url = dep_serve_url(resolved, &state.root);
+                return Redirect::temporary(&url).into_response();
+            }
             return (StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, format!("oj: no plugin loaded {id}")).into_response();
         }
         Err(e) => return (StatusCode::INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, e).into_response(),
